      "text": "To solve the expression \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\), we can use the tangent addition formula and some trigonometric identities. Let's proceed step by step.\n\nFirst, recall the tangent addition formula:\n\\[\n\\tan(A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}\n\\]\nWe will use this formula in a strategic way. Notice that \\(20^\\circ + 25^\\circ = 45^\\circ\\). So, we can rewrite the given expression using the value of \\(\\tan 45^\\circ\\).\n\nSince \\(\\tan 45^\\circ = 1\\), we can rewrite the expression as:\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1^2 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nThis can be seen as:\n\\[\n1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = \\tan 45^\\circ = 1\n\\]\nTherefore, we have:\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1\n\\]\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]",
