      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We can use the tangent addition formula to simplify this expression.\nRecall that $\\tan(a + b) = \\frac{\\tan a + \\tan b}{1 - \\tan a \\tan b}$.\nUsing this, let $a = 20^\\circ$ and $b = 25^\\circ$.\nThen $\\tan(45^\\circ) = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}$.\nSince $\\tan 45^\\circ = 1$, we have $1 = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}$.\nMultiplying both sides by $(1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ)$ gives $1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ$.\nAdding these two expressions together gives us $1 + \\tan 25^\\circ - \\tan 20^\\circ = 2 \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ$.\nFinally, using the tangent addition formula again, we have $\\tan(45^\\circ) = \\frac{1 + \\tan 25^\\circ - \\tan 20^\\circ}{1 - (1)(\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ) + 1} = \\frac{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ - \\tan 25^\\circ}{-2 \\tan 20^\\circ - \\tan 25^\\circ}$.\nSimplifying the numerator and denominator, we get $\\frac{1 + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ}{-\\tan 20^\\circ - \\tan 25^\\circ} = \\frac{\\tan 35^\\circ}{-\\tan 45^\\circ}$.\nSince $\\tan 35^\\circ = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ and $\\tan 45^\\circ = 1$, we have $\\frac{\\tan 35^\\circ}{-\\tan 45^\\circ} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}}{-1} = \\frac{(-\\sqrt{3})}{3} = \\boxed{-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}$.\nThe answer is: -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}",
